她可不想生病。

792
00:33:28.210 --> 00:33:30.670
Don't you so wish you had that now?
你现在是不是特别希望自己也有一个？

793
00:33:30.810 --> 00:33:32.190
Man, oh, man.
天哪，天哪。

794
00:33:32.250 --> 00:33:33.950
I wish I had it.
我真希望我有。

795
00:33:34.050 --> 00:33:35.630
I've been asked that so many times.
这个问题我被问过太多次了。

796
00:33:35.870 --> 00:33:43.450
Well, listen, Erin says she's a little bit sick, but she's trying to push through because she just does not want to miss her date with Andy.
听着，Erin说她有点生病了，但她想坚持下去，因为她不想错过和Andy的约会。

797
00:33:43.450 --> 00:33:44.590
It's so sweet.
太甜了。

798
00:33:45.150 --> 00:33:47.650
We got a fan question from Catherine D.
我们收到了一位来自俄勒冈州波特兰的粉丝Catherine D的提问。

799
00:33:47.910 --> 00:33:49.010
in Portland, Oregon.
来自俄勒冈州波特兰。

800
00:33:49.010 --> 00:33:54.650
And was Ellie Kemper actually sick in this episode, or is she faking her congested voice?
Ellie Kemper在这一集中是真的生病了，还是她装出了那种鼻音？

801
00:33:55.290 --> 00:33:57.090
She is faking, you guys.
她在装病，伙计们。

802
00:33:57.290 --> 00:33:57.950
I mean...
我是说……

803
00:33:57.950 --> 00:34:00.030
It's some great sick performance work.
这表演真是病得不轻。

804
00:34:00.050 --> 00:34:02.290
It's some great fakey cold work right there.
这装病装得真是太到位了。

805
00:34:02.350 --> 00:34:03.050
Really good.
演得真好。

806
00:34:03.570 --> 00:34:07.170
I was perplexed by what Erin shared in her talking head.
艾琳在采访中说的话让我很困惑。

807
00:34:07.170 --> 00:34:15.230
And she said she usually recovers when she's sick in just a few hours, except for the time she was in a hospital from ages three to six.
她说她生病通常几个小时就能好，除了三岁到六岁那次住院经历之外。

808
00:34:15.470 --> 00:34:15.830
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

809
00:34:16.090 --> 00:34:20.970
We are learning so many random things about people's backstory in this episode.
这一集我们了解到了好多关于大家背景故事的琐事。

810
00:34:21.110 --> 00:34:21.950
We really are.
确实如此。

811
00:34:22.670 --> 00:34:26.510
Well, now it is time for Jo's town hall.
好了，现在是乔的市政厅会议时间了。

812
00:34:26.690 --> 00:34:31.230
She gathers everyone in the bullpen, and she says, I want to hear your ideas.
她把大家召集到办公区，说，我想听听你们的想法。

813
00:34:31.510 --> 00:34:36.830
She's been hearing ideas from executives, but she wants to hear from everyone.
她之前一直在听高管们的想法，但她想听听所有人的意见。

814
00:34:37.150 --> 00:34:43.090
She says, I mean, did you guys know that liquid paper, that wasn't invented by some fancy engineer?
她说，我是说，你们知道吗，修正液可不是什么高级工程师发明的？

815
00:34:43.090 --> 00:34:45.830
No, that was created by a lowly typiSt.
不，那是一个卑微的打字员发明的。

816
00:34:46.250 --> 00:34:47.990
Well, Kevin chimes in right away.
凯文立刻插话了。

817
00:34:47.990 --> 00:34:51.990
He says, well, I have an idea for a suntan lotion soap.
他说，嗯，我有个关于防晒乳液肥皂的点子。

818
00:34:52.390 --> 00:34:55.330
And Jo says, doesn't have to be an invention, Kevin.
乔说，不一定非得是发明，凯文。

819
00:34:56.050 --> 00:34:59.110
Jenna, there were so many alts for that line.
珍娜，那句台词有好多备选方案。

820
00:34:59.250 --> 00:34:59.550
What?
什么？

821
00:34:59.990 --> 00:35:01.730
For suntan lotion soap?
关于防晒乳液肥皂的？

822
00:35:01.870 --> 00:35:06.850
I went to the candy bag alts for Kevin's suntan lotion soap.
我翻到了凯文防晒乳液肥皂的备选方案。

823
00:35:06.950 --> 00:35:07.710
Oh, I'm dying.
天哪，我要笑死了。

824
00:35:07.930 --> 00:35:08.910
I literally can't wait.
我简直迫不及待了。

825
00:35:09.090 --> 00:35:10.010
I mean, look how many.
我是说，看看有多少个。

826
00:35:10.170 --> 00:35:10.810
Oh, my God.
天哪。

827
00:35:10.890 --> 00:35:11.410
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

828
00:35:11.550 --> 00:35:12.770
Okay, here we go.
好了，我们开始吧。

829
00:35:12.770 --> 00:35:16.230
I can just see right now the writers up in the writer's room.
我能想象出编剧们在编剧室里的样子。

830
00:35:16.390 --> 00:35:17.690
Pitching like crazy.
疯狂地提出各种点子。

831
00:35:17.690 --> 00:35:19.910
Cracking up over what are Kevin's inventions.
为了凯文的那些发明笑得前仰后合。

832
00:35:20.190 --> 00:35:22.010
Okay, here are the alts.
好了，这是备选方案。

833
00:35:22.330 --> 00:35:25.470
A hook that you put all your keys on so you don't lose them.
一个可以挂所有钥匙的钩子，这样你就不会弄丢它们了。

834
00:35:25.610 --> 00:35:25.970
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

835
00:35:26.470 --> 00:35:27.230
Face hat.
脸部帽子。

836
00:35:27.430 --> 00:35:29.210
I don't know exactly what it's for.
我不太确定那是干什么用的。

837
00:35:29.430 --> 00:35:32.170
A device that turns any sink into a urinal.
一个能把任何水槽变成小便池的装置。

838
00:35:33.190 --> 00:35:34.750
Charcoal-filtered underwear.
活性炭过滤内裤。

839
00:35:35.350 --> 00:35:37.490
Remote-controlled sack adjuster.
遥控式裤裆调节器。

840
00:35:38.390 --> 00:35:39.510
Orgasm detector.
高潮探测器。

841
00:35:40.330 --> 00:35:41.030
Babe magnet.
美女磁铁。

842
00:35:41.430 --> 00:35:43.150
The never-ending French fry.
永远吃不完的炸薯条。

843
00:35:43.510 --> 00:35:45.490
An app that invents apps.
一个能发明应用程序的应用程序。

844
00:35:46.110 --> 00:35:48.130
What about an invention that makes inventions?
发明一个能发明东西的发明怎么样？

845
00:35:48.130 --> 00:35:50.610
Because then you just make that and you're home free.
因为只要做成那个，你就万事大吉了。

846
00:35:52.150 --> 00:35:53.450
I have an invention.
我有一个发明。

847
00:35:53.870 --> 00:35:55.570
Pants with a built-in chair.
自带椅子的裤子。

848
00:35:55.730 --> 00:35:57.450
So you always have a place to sit.
这样你随时都有地方坐。

849
00:35:57.690 --> 00:36:01.910
I got the idea from a time when I got stuck in a chair and just went with it.
这个点子源于有一次我被椅子卡住，干脆就顺其自然了。

850
00:36:02.070 --> 00:36:02.450
Wait.
等等。

851
00:36:02.650 --> 00:36:03.910
That's Michael's invention.
那是迈克尔的发明。

852
00:36:04.190 --> 00:36:04.650
I know.
我知道。

853
00:36:04.850 --> 00:36:07.650
I want to see that scene where Michael gets really angry.
我想看迈克尔真正生气的那一幕。

854
00:36:07.650 --> 00:36:09.110
Where he's like, that's my invention.
就是他说“那是我的发明”的那种。

855
00:36:09.110 --> 00:36:10.890
They talk about it at company picnic.
他们在公司野餐会上谈论过这件事。

856
00:36:11.050 --> 00:36:11.530
I know.
我知道。

857
00:36:11.970 --> 00:36:12.530
Okay.
好吧。

858
00:36:12.830 --> 00:36:13.650
Next one.
下一个。

859
00:36:14.110 --> 00:36:17.870
They have 3D glasses, but do they have ID glasses?
他们有3D眼镜，但他们有身份识别眼镜吗？

860
00:36:18.590 --> 00:36:19.070
Hmm.
嗯。

861
00:36:19.350 --> 00:36:22.850
I feel like that's probably something that is about to roll out.
我觉得这大概是即将推出的产品。

862
00:36:22.970 --> 00:36:23.310
Perhaps.
也许吧。

863
00:36:24.110 --> 00:36:25.610
Dog biscuits for people.
给人类吃的狗饼干。

864
00:36:26.330 --> 00:36:28.770
A game that lets you be a swan.
一款让你扮演天鹅的游戏。

865
00:36:29.450 --> 00:36:30.070
Huh.
哈。

866
00:36:30.370 --> 00:36:33.010
A bicycle powered by licking a lollipop.
靠舔棒棒糖驱动的自行车。

867
00:36:33.670 --> 00:36:36.470
An app that lists all your condiments.
一款列出你所有调味品的应用程序。

868
00:36:37.230 --> 00:36:38.990
What would you need that app for?
你需要那个应用程序做什么？

869
00:36:39.290 --> 00:36:43.150
I don't know, but there would be some controversy over what a condiment is.
我不知道，但关于什么是调味品，肯定会引起一些争议。

870
00:36:43.550 --> 00:36:43.710
Yes.
是的。

871
00:36:44.550 --> 00:36:47.750
Those were all of Kevin's suntan lotion soap alts.
那些都是凯文关于防晒霜肥皂的备选方案。

872
00:36:47.910 --> 00:36:51.250
I felt like some of those sounded like Michael Scott inventions.
我觉得其中一些听起来像是迈克尔·斯科特的发明。

873
00:36:51.670 --> 00:36:51.850
Yeah.
是啊。

874
00:36:52.130 --> 00:36:56.350
But the one that sounded most Kevin to me was never-ending french fry.
但我觉得最像凯文风格的是“永远吃不完的炸薯条”。

875
00:36:57.010 --> 00:36:57.570
Yes.
没错。

876
00:36:57.790 --> 00:37:00.750
Also, maybe the remote-controlled sack adjuster.
还有，也许是遥控式蛋蛋调整器。

877
00:37:01.250 --> 00:37:04.290
Does that mean something adjusts your balls remotely?
那是指有什么东西可以远程调整你的蛋蛋吗？

878
00:37:04.290 --> 00:37:06.850
So you don't have to lean down and touch them.
这样你就不用弯腰去碰它们了。

879
00:37:06.950 --> 00:37:07.150
Right.
对。

880
00:37:07.610 --> 00:37:09.050
Should you be in public?
如果你在公共场合呢？

881
00:37:09.290 --> 00:37:09.470
Yeah.
是啊。

882
00:37:09.590 --> 00:37:10.870
You hit your little remote button.
你按下你的小遥控按钮。

883
00:37:10.970 --> 00:37:11.050
Yeah.
嗯。

884
00:37:11.050 --> 00:37:12.170
And it shifts your balls around.
然后它就会帮你调整蛋蛋的位置。

885
00:37:12.370 --> 00:37:12.970
It does it for you.
它会替你完成。

886
00:37:13.030 --> 00:37:13.670
Well, there you go.
好吧，这不就成了嘛。

887
00:37:14.050 --> 00:37:19.410
Well, I got very interested in Joe's comment about the inventor of liquid paper.
嗯，我对乔关于涂改液发明者的评论非常感兴趣。

888
00:37:19.930 --> 00:37:21.030
Did you deep dive?
你深入研究了吗？

889
00:37:21.350 --> 00:37:22.410
Yes, I did, Angela.
是的，安吉拉，我研究了。

890
00:37:22.670 --> 00:37:24.630
And this story is amazing.
而且这个故事太棒了。

891
00:37:25.330 --> 00:37:28.910
Liquid paper was invented by Bette Nesmith Graham.
涂改液是由贝蒂·内史密斯·格雷厄姆发明的。

892
00:37:30.090 --> 00:37:37.990
In 1954, she was a divorced single mom supporting herself and her son as a secretary working at a bank in Texas.
1954年，她是一位离异的单身母亲，在德克萨斯州的一家银行当秘书，靠微薄的薪水养活自己和儿子。

893
00:37:37.990 --> 00:37:40.230
She made about $300 a month.
她每月大约挣300美元。

894
00:37:40.630 --> 00:37:41.550
Here's the thing, though.
不过重点来了。

895
00:37:41.910 --> 00:37:44.050
She was a really bad typiSt.
她是个打字非常糟糕的人。

896
00:37:44.170 --> 00:37:49.850
And every time she had to correct her mistakes, you either had to kind of, like, erase it and then it would smudge.
每次她不得不纠正错误时，要么得擦掉，结果弄得一团糟。

897
00:37:49.850 --> 00:37:52.470
Or you'd just have to start all over again.
要么就得从头再来。

898
00:37:52.970 --> 00:37:55.350
Well, she was also a painter.
嗯，她同时也是一位画家。

899
00:37:55.670 --> 00:38:02.830
And she thought to herself, you know, when painters make a mistake, they don't erase it or they don't start over.
她心想，你知道，当画家犯错时，他们不会擦掉，也不会从头再来。

900
00:38:03.050 --> 00:38:04.450
They just paint over it.
他们只是在上面重新画一遍。

901
00:38:04.690 --> 00:38:14.870
So she was like, what if I took some of my white tempura paint to work and I painted over my mistakes and I let it dry and then I typed over it?
于是她想，如果我带些白色蛋彩颜料去上班，把写错的地方涂掉，等它干了再重新打字会怎样？

902
00:38:15.350 --> 00:38:16.230
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

903
00:38:16.430 --> 00:38:17.750
It freaking worked.
居然真的成功了。

904
00:38:18.750 --> 00:38:23.610
But she was like, I need to make a better formula than just this straight paint.
但她觉得，我得调配出比这种纯颜料更好的配方。

905
00:38:23.830 --> 00:38:29.650
So in her kitchen at home with her blender, she created liquid paper.
于是她在自家的厨房里，用搅拌机发明了修正液。

906
00:38:29.850 --> 00:38:33.090
She put it in little nail polish bottles.
她把它装进小小的指甲油瓶里。

907
00:38:33.450 --> 00:38:33.970
Brilliant.
太聪明了。

908
00:38:34.450 --> 00:38:38.750
And for five years, she and her coworkers at the bank used it.
接下来的五年里，她和银行的同事们一直在用它。

909
00:38:38.830 --> 00:38:40.010
They called it mistake out.
他们管它叫“错误消除剂”。

910
00:38:40.950 --> 00:38:44.470
Well, then she got the idea, I should do something with this.
后来她萌生了一个想法：我应该用它做点什么。

911
00:38:44.590 --> 00:38:45.270
Yes, you should.
没错，确实应该。

912
00:38:45.390 --> 00:38:46.230
I'm going to make this a business.
我要把它做成一门生意。

913
00:38:46.230 --> 00:38:51.590
So she hired some teenagers for a dollar an hour to package it up in her garage.
于是她雇了一些青少年，每小时一美元，在车库里进行包装。

914
00:38:51.590 --> 00:38:54.270
And they started shipping it out and sending it to places.
他们开始把它发往各地。

915
00:38:54.610 --> 00:38:56.170
She applied for a patent.
她申请了专利。

916
00:38:56.390 --> 00:38:57.510
It caught on.
它火了起来。

917
00:38:57.670 --> 00:38:59.430
She renamed it liquid paper.
她把它重新命名为“修正液”。

918
00:38:59.430 --> 00:39:04.090
And they started opening up factories in Dallas, Toronto, and Brussels.
他们开始在达拉斯、多伦多和布鲁塞尔开设工厂。

919
00:39:04.510 --> 00:39:10.570
At its peak, they were making 25 million bottles of liquid paper every year.
在鼎盛时期，他们每年生产2500万瓶修正液。

920
00:39:10.870 --> 00:39:13.830
With her wealth, she established two foundations.
凭借积累的财富，她成立了两个基金会。

921
00:39:14.150 --> 00:39:20.490
One that gave grants and financial support to promote women in the arts and the other which supported women in business.
一个用于资助和支持女性从事艺术，另一个则支持女性创业。

922
00:39:21.270 --> 00:39:26.370
But at one point, while her liquid paper business is booming, she decided to get married again.
但在修正液生意蒸蒸日上的时候，她决定再次结婚。

923
00:39:26.810 --> 00:39:28.590
But guess what this guy did?
但你猜这个男人做了什么？

924
00:39:28.970 --> 00:39:31.490
Please don't tell me he took her money or sold her patent.
千万别告诉我他卷走了她的钱或者卖掉了她的专利。

925
00:39:31.710 --> 00:39:32.610
Please don't tell me.
千万别告诉我。

926
00:39:32.730 --> 00:39:37.770
He tried to push her out of her own company and take it over for himself.
他试图把她踢出公司，自己接管一切。

927
00:39:38.350 --> 00:39:39.730
What a S-O-B.
真是个混蛋。

928
00:39:39.730 --> 00:39:40.750
That's right.
没错。

929
00:39:41.090 --> 00:39:46.270
He even tried to change the formula of liquid paper ever so slightly so that—
他甚至试图稍微改动一下修正液的配方，以便——

930
00:39:46.270 --> 00:39:47.290
So he could patent it himself.
以便他能自己申请专利。

931
00:39:47.470 --> 00:39:49.870
So that he wouldn't have to pay her royalties on it.
这样他就不用再付给她专利使用费了。

932
00:39:50.150 --> 00:39:51.170
Well, guess what?
结果呢，你猜怎么着？

933
00:39:51.330 --> 00:39:52.450
She prevailed.
她赢了。

934
00:39:52.610 --> 00:39:57.230
She sold the company in 1979 for $47.5 million.
1979年，她以4750万美元的价格卖掉了公司。

935
00:39:57.310 --> 00:39:59.950
She gave millions of dollars to charity.
她捐出了数百万美元用于慈善事业。

936
00:40:00.550 --> 00:40:05.270
Sadly, she died six months later from a stroke after selling her company.
遗憾的是，她在卖掉公司六个月后因中风去世了。

937
00:40:06.270 --> 00:40:12.470
And incidentally, her son is Michael Nesmith, the guitarist for The Monkees.
顺便提一下，她的儿子是“顽童合唱团”的吉他手迈克尔·内史密斯。

938
00:40:12.750 --> 00:40:14.390
The rock band The Monkees.
就是那个摇滚乐队“顽童合唱团”。

939
00:40:14.470 --> 00:40:15.150
It's his mom.
那是他妈妈。

940
00:40:15.650 --> 00:40:17.290
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

941
00:40:17.470 --> 00:40:17.770
Right?
对吧？

942
00:40:18.110 --> 00:40:20.110
That is a fascinating story.
这真是一个引人入胜的故事。

943
00:40:20.390 --> 00:40:21.930
I loved that story.
我太喜欢这个故事了。

944
00:40:22.070 --> 00:40:22.470
Me too.
我也是。

945
00:40:22.770 --> 00:40:26.550
It's just a person solving a problem in their everyday life, you know?
这就像是一个普通人在日常生活中解决了一个问题，你懂吗？

946
00:40:26.810 --> 00:40:28.170
That's like my friend.
就像我的朋友一样。

947
00:40:28.410 --> 00:40:29.690
Oh, the cupcake lady.
哦，那个做纸杯蛋糕的女士吗？

948
00:40:29.910 --> 00:40:30.410
Yes.
是的。

949
00:40:30.710 --> 00:40:32.310
My friend, Jennifer Gunn.
我的朋友，詹妮弗·冈恩。

950
00:40:32.530 --> 00:40:33.910
She was a stay-at-home mom.
她曾经是一位全职妈妈。

951
00:40:33.910 --> 00:40:37.770
She's constantly making cupcakes for her kids to take to school.
她总是给孩子们做纸杯蛋糕带去学校。

952
00:40:37.770 --> 00:40:40.470
And she was annoyed that they were getting all messed up.
她很苦恼，因为蛋糕总是弄得一团糟。

953
00:40:40.690 --> 00:40:43.450
She's like, I can't keep putting them in like a shirt box.
她说，我不能老是把它们装在衬衫盒之类的盒子里。

954
00:40:43.570 --> 00:40:45.030
What am I transporting them in?
我该用什么来装它们呢？

955
00:40:45.510 --> 00:40:47.850
So she came up with the cupcake courier.
于是她发明了纸杯蛋糕快递盒。

956
00:40:48.190 --> 00:40:49.490
And she patented it.
她还申请了专利。

957
00:40:49.590 --> 00:40:52.250
And she sold it out of her garage for years.
多年来，她一直在自家车库里售卖这款产品。

958
00:40:52.430 --> 00:40:54.570
And then finally, she sold the design.
最后，她把设计卖掉了。

959
00:40:54.570 --> 00:40:56.730
And it's in like Target and all these places.
现在塔吉特百货和很多地方都有卖。

960
00:40:56.870 --> 00:40:57.290
Yeah, you get it everywhere.
没错，到处都能买到。

961
00:40:57.510 --> 00:40:58.410
Bed, Bath, and Beyond.
Bed, Bath, and Beyond也有。

962
00:40:59.270 --> 00:40:59.670
Amazing.
太棒了。

963
00:41:00.010 --> 00:41:02.490
When she told me, I was like, how has no one thought of this before?
她告诉我的时候，我就想，怎么以前没人想到这个呢？

964
00:41:02.490 --> 00:41:06.710
It was this amazing, like, stackable cupcake transportation device.
那是一个非常棒的、可堆叠的纸杯蛋糕运输装置。

965
00:41:06.910 --> 00:41:07.710
Josh has one.
乔什有一个。

966
00:41:07.750 --> 00:41:08.350
I know.
我知道。

967
00:41:08.630 --> 00:41:10.130
I brought it on Rachel Ray.
我把它带到了雷切尔·雷的节目上。

968
00:41:10.370 --> 00:41:11.430
I was so excited about it.
我当时兴奋极了。

969
00:41:11.490 --> 00:41:12.110
I was like, give me one.
我说，给我一个。

970
00:41:12.230 --> 00:41:14.630
I'm giving one to Rachel Ray when I go on her talk show.
我要去上雷切尔·雷的脱口秀，我要送她一个。

971
00:41:15.490 --> 00:41:16.310
Cupcake courier.
纸杯蛋糕快递盒。

972
00:41:16.510 --> 00:41:17.170
Liquid paper.
修正液。

973
00:41:17.710 --> 00:41:18.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

974
00:41:18.250 --> 00:41:18.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

975
00:41:19.490 --> 00:41:21.110
Women solving everyday probleMs.
女性解决日常难题。

976
00:41:21.390 --> 00:41:21.510
Yeah.
没错。

977
00:41:22.070 --> 00:41:28.690
During this town hall meeting, I have to point out how great they build this irritation that
在这次市政厅会议期间，我必须指出他们把乔对迈克尔的那种恼火感营造得有多棒。

978
00:41:28.690 --> 00:41:30.030
Joe has towards Michael.
乔对迈克尔的恼火。

979
00:41:30.290 --> 00:41:33.210
Well, he keeps, like, doing all these, like, sidebars.
嗯，他总是搞这些小动作。

980
00:41:33.370 --> 00:41:36.370
Like, he does when anyone else ever is running a meeting.
就像别人开会时他也会那样。

981
00:41:37.110 --> 00:41:40.250
But one person is going to shine in this meeting, and it's Daryl.
但这次会议中有一个人会大放异彩，那就是达里尔。

982
00:41:40.370 --> 00:41:44.230
He has an idea about shipment because printers and paper ship differently.
他有一个关于运输的想法，因为打印机和纸张的运输方式不同。

983
00:41:44.570 --> 00:41:44.910
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

984
00:41:44.910 --> 00:41:47.290
And he shows this to Joe, and she's like, I like this.
他把这个想法展示给乔看，她说，我喜欢这个。

985
00:41:47.370 --> 00:41:48.790
You should have an office up here.
你应该在这里有个办公室。

986
00:41:49.470 --> 00:41:49.890
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

987
00:41:49.890 --> 00:41:51.870
And then her dynamic with Gabe is so great.
还有她和盖博之间的互动真是太棒了。

988
00:41:51.950 --> 00:41:52.650
It's so good.
太精彩了。

989
00:41:52.910 --> 00:41:54.590
Gabe was like, I actually put, you know what?
盖博当时说，我真的，你知道吗？

990
00:41:54.590 --> 00:41:55.490
I'm going to pack up my stuff.
我要收拾东西走人了。

991
00:41:55.650 --> 00:41:55.950
No problem.
没问题。

992
00:41:56.250 --> 00:41:56.650
Exactly.
没错。

993
00:41:57.630 --> 00:42:02.990
And this is the moment Michael reveals that he bought tickets to come to Tallahassee.
这一刻，迈克尔透露他买了去塔拉哈西的机票。

994
00:42:03.310 --> 00:42:04.950
July 4th weekend.
七月四号那个周末。

995
00:42:05.510 --> 00:42:06.490
July 4th weekend.
七月四号那个周末。

996
00:42:06.610 --> 00:42:08.590
But not only that, there's multiple.
不仅如此，还不止一张。

997
00:42:08.870 --> 00:42:09.710
He booked multiple.
他订了好几张。

998
00:42:09.970 --> 00:42:11.930
Just in case July 4th didn't work out.
以防七月四号那天去不成。

999
00:42:11.930 --> 00:42:14.430
And Joe's like, no, no, no, you didn't do that.
乔说，不，不，不，你没这么做吧。

1000
00:42:14.450 --> 00:42:15.410
I'm off and not home.
我不在家，也不在办公室。

1001
00:42:15.530 --> 00:42:16.550
It's getting so awkward.
气氛变得越来越尴尬了。

1002
00:42:16.890 --> 00:42:18.350
Michael isn't catching the hint.
迈克尔完全没领会到暗示。

1003
00:42:18.550 --> 00:42:20.190
And finally, she's like, enough!
最后，她终于忍无可忍了！

1004
00:42:20.670 --> 00:42:22.530
Jenna, I remember when we filmed that.
珍娜，我记得我们拍那场戏的时候。

1005
00:42:22.630 --> 00:42:22.970
You do?
真的吗？

1006
00:42:23.210 --> 00:42:24.490
You could have heard a pin drop.
当时安静得连根针掉在地上都能听见。

1007
00:42:25.330 --> 00:42:26.850
We were all terrified.
我们当时都吓坏了。

1008
00:42:28.190 --> 00:42:30.830
She was so powerful in that moment.
那一刻她的气场太强大了。

1009
00:42:31.390 --> 00:42:33.330
Like, her acting is so good.
她的演技真的太棒了。

1010
00:42:33.530 --> 00:42:35.430
It literally shut up the whole room.
整个房间瞬间鸦雀无声。

1011
00:42:35.810 --> 00:42:36.690
I love her.
我爱死她了。

1012
00:42:37.650 --> 00:42:43.130
And Michael has this line where he says, all right, everybody, just try to put a brave face on.
迈克尔有句台词是这么说的：好了，各位，尽量表现得坚强一点。

1013
00:42:43.970 --> 00:42:45.830
It looks like he's about to cry.
他看起来快要哭出来了。

1014
00:42:47.110 --> 00:42:50.310
Daryl is moving on up to his new office.
达里尔正要搬进他的新办公室。

1015
00:42:50.530 --> 00:42:51.090
He's singing.
他在唱歌。

1016
00:42:51.290 --> 00:42:52.490
The jingle from the Jeffersons.
唱的是《杰斐逊一家》的主题曲。

1017
00:42:53.010 --> 00:42:55.110
Yes, it was written by Janet Dubois.
没错，那是珍妮特·杜波依斯写的。

1018
00:42:55.110 --> 00:43:03.570
Randy negotiated just the sync rights to the song, which meant that Craig could sing them a cappella, but could have no musical accompaniment,
兰迪只谈下了这首歌的同步权，这意味着克雷格可以清唱，但不能有任何音乐伴奏，

1019
00:43:03.650 --> 00:43:05.490
and we could not play the actual song.
而且我们不能播放原曲。

1020
00:43:05.670 --> 00:43:11.830
And it cost us $17,000 for him to sing as he's moving into his new office.
为了让他搬进新办公室时唱那几句，我们花了17000美元。

1021
00:43:12.350 --> 00:43:14.130
Michael is confused.
迈克尔很困惑。

1022
00:43:14.590 --> 00:43:15.550
He's upset.
他很心烦。

1023
00:43:15.770 --> 00:43:17.390
He goes in to see Joe.
他去找乔了。

1024
00:43:18.050 --> 00:43:25.090
I love when he's like, I'll knock once for yes and twice for no, and she said, how many knocks to get you to do some work?
我喜欢他那句：我敲一下代表是，敲两下代表否。然后她说：你要敲多少下才能开始干活？

1025
00:43:25.230 --> 00:43:25.790
I know.
我知道。

1026
00:43:26.270 --> 00:43:27.170
It's so good.
太精彩了。

1027
00:43:27.570 --> 00:43:29.450
Well, lady, I think we should take a break.
好吧，女士，我觉得我们该休息一下了。

1028
00:43:29.610 --> 00:43:32.230
I do, too, because when we come back, the cat's in the cradle.
我也这么觉得，因为回来之后，就要放《猫在摇篮里》了。

1029
00:43:32.610 --> 00:43:32.990
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1030
00:43:33.510 --> 00:43:34.390
Jim is feeling guilty.
吉姆感到很内疚。

1031
00:43:34.590 --> 00:43:35.710
Dwight's plan is working.
德怀特的计划奏效了。

1032
00:43:36.350 --> 00:43:37.150
It's working.
确实奏效了。

1033
00:44:03.560 --> 00:44:08.180
This is the song that Dwight is playing while Jim is on a sales call.
这就是吉姆在打销售电话时，德怀特放的那首歌。

1034
00:44:08.800 --> 00:44:09.200
Yeah.
没错。

1035
00:44:09.860 --> 00:44:11.400
I can't listen to that song.
我听不了这首歌。

1036
00:44:11.400 --> 00:44:13.020
It makes me too sad.
它让我太难过了。

1037
00:44:13.180 --> 00:44:13.960
I'm so sorry.
真抱歉。

1038
00:44:13.960 --> 00:44:15.520
I just had Sam play it.
我刚才还让萨姆放了这首歌。

1039
00:44:15.840 --> 00:44:17.540
I can't listen to the whole thing.
我没法听完整首歌。

1040
00:44:17.740 --> 00:44:19.120
It bums me out too much.
它让我太沮丧了。

1041
00:44:20.080 --> 00:44:24.240
Cats in the Cradle is a 1974 folk rock song by Harry Chapin.
《猫在摇篮里》是哈里·查平在1974年创作的一首民谣摇滚歌曲。

1042
00:44:24.540 --> 00:44:26.160
I did not know this.
我之前不知道这个。

1043
00:44:26.420 --> 00:44:35.040
The song began as a poem written by his wife, Sandy, inspired by her ex-husband's awkward relationship with his father.
这首歌最初是他妻子桑迪写的一首诗，灵感来源于她前夫与父亲之间尴尬的关系。

1044
00:44:36.420 --> 00:44:40.860
Chapin said the song is also about his own relationship with his son, Josh.
查平说这首歌也关于他自己与儿子乔什的关系。

1045
00:44:41.400 --> 00:44:41.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1046
00:44:42.440 --> 00:44:50.200
Basically, I think you guys know what the song is about, but the reason Dwight's playing it is because it's about a man who becomes a father,
基本上，我想你们都知道这首歌讲的是什么，但德怀特放这首歌的原因是，它讲的是一个男人当了父亲，

1047
00:44:50.200 --> 00:44:55.920
but he's just too busy to spend time with his son, and his son's always asking him, spend time with me.
但他总是太忙，没时间陪儿子，而儿子总是求他：陪陪我吧。

1048
00:44:55.920 --> 00:44:58.320
And the dad's like, we'll find a good time later.
而父亲总是说：以后我们再找时间吧。

1049
00:44:58.520 --> 00:44:58.720
Yeah.
没错。

1050
00:44:58.900 --> 00:45:05.100
But then in the final verse, the son is all grown up, and the dad finally wants to spend time with him, but now the son is too busy.
但到了最后一段，儿子长大了，父亲终于想花时间陪他了，可现在儿子却太忙了。

1051
00:45:05.480 --> 00:45:11.580
And he realizes his son has grown up to be just like him, just too busy for relationship and intimacy.
他意识到儿子长得和他一模一样，忙得没时间经营感情和亲密关系。

1052
00:45:11.580 --> 00:45:15.600
This song makes me sad, and so does the book, The Giving Tree.
这首歌让我很难过，那本《爱心树》也是。

1053
00:45:15.840 --> 00:45:16.740
Always makes me sad.
总是让我很难过。

1054
00:45:17.000 --> 00:45:17.980
Oh, right?
噢，是吗？

1055
00:45:18.260 --> 00:45:18.480
Ugh.
呃。

1056
00:45:19.840 --> 00:45:28.680
Randy told me that we had to pay for both the sync and the master rates to this song because we both hear the song, and then Dwight and Andy sing it,
兰迪告诉我，我们必须支付这首歌的同步费和母带费，因为我们不仅听到了这首歌，德怀特和安迪还唱了它，

1057
00:45:28.740 --> 00:45:32.280
and the total cost for this was $46,000.
总费用是46000美元。

1058
00:45:32.860 --> 00:45:42.860
Well, Jim is going to have a talking head, like you said, outside of Vance Refrigeration, and he's going to say he's not surprised that Dwight is using his baby to steal his desk,
吉姆会有一个单人采访，就像你说的，在万斯制冷公司外面，他会说他不惊讶德怀特利用他的孩子来抢他的办公桌，

1059
00:45:42.920 --> 00:45:45.440
but what he is surprised by is that it's working.
但他惊讶的是这招竟然奏效了。

1060
00:45:45.920 --> 00:45:51.940
This next scene, Erin is going to bring Joe a fax, but she's so clearly sick.
下一场戏，艾琳要给乔送传真，但她明显病得很重。

1061
00:45:52.320 --> 00:45:58.820
Joe's reaction to Erin walking in the room sick, she's like, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, get out.
乔看到艾琳生病走进房间的反应是，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，出去。

1062
00:45:59.420 --> 00:46:01.400
It made me laugh really hard.
这让我笑得很大声。

1063
00:46:01.400 --> 00:46:04.060
Lady, am I, seriously, am I Joe Bennett?
天哪，我是，说真的，我是乔·贝内特吗？

1064
00:46:04.060 --> 00:46:05.100
I think you might be.
我觉得你可能是。

1065
00:46:05.220 --> 00:46:08.720
That is 100% how I react to a sick person walking into a room.
这百分之百是我看到生病的人走进房间时的反应。

1066
00:46:08.820 --> 00:46:10.820
I'm like, oh, wait, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.
我会说，噢，等等，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不，不。

1067
00:46:11.080 --> 00:46:12.560
Hi, not today.
嗨，今天不行。

1068
00:46:12.960 --> 00:46:15.300
I am not getting sick today because of you.
我今天可不会因为你而生病。

1069
00:46:15.540 --> 00:46:16.800
You need to go home.
你需要回家。

1070
00:46:17.360 --> 00:46:19.320
I was like that before the pandemic.
我在疫情前就是这样了。

1071
00:46:19.580 --> 00:46:21.600
I know, and now you're really leaning into it.
我知道，现在你更是变本加厉了。

1072
00:46:21.640 --> 00:46:22.460
I really am.
确实是。

1073
00:46:22.660 --> 00:46:24.260
Like, sniffle, goodbye.
比如，吸吸鼻子，再见。

1074
00:46:24.420 --> 00:46:25.080
Don't think so.
我不这么认为。

1075
00:46:25.860 --> 00:46:29.800
Well, Andy is super bummed out because Joe sends Erin home,
安迪非常沮丧，因为乔把艾琳打发回家了，

1076
00:46:30.640 --> 00:46:32.900
and now what are they going to do about their date?
现在他们该怎么处理约会的事呢？

1077
00:46:33.760 --> 00:46:35.160
Well, Andy has an idea.
安迪有个主意。

1078
00:46:36.040 --> 00:46:37.500
He's going to go in to Joe.
他要去找乔。

1079
00:46:37.760 --> 00:46:41.380
He's going to have a bunch of coughing and a bunch of sickie.
他要装出一大堆咳嗽和生病的样子。

1080
00:46:42.140 --> 00:46:43.460
Joe's going to send him home.
乔就会把他打发回家。

1081
00:46:44.660 --> 00:46:46.560
Everyone should have started hacking and coughing.
每个人都应该开始大声咳嗽。

1082
00:46:46.800 --> 00:46:48.200
They all would have gotten to go to the bar.
他们就都能去酒吧了。

1083
00:46:48.400 --> 00:46:49.360
You're so right.
你说得太对了。

1084
00:46:50.120 --> 00:46:53.140
Angela, have you ever pretended to be sick to get out of something?
安吉拉，你有没有为了逃避某事而假装生病过？

1085
00:46:53.420 --> 00:46:55.140
Oh, my gosh, you're putting me on the spot.
天哪，你这是在让我难堪。

1086
00:46:55.140 --> 00:46:56.180
I'm sure I have.
我肯定有过。

1087
00:46:56.780 --> 00:46:57.480
You know what?
你知道吗？

1088
00:46:57.600 --> 00:47:00.840
One of the things that just comes to mind, which is so lame, Jenna,
我脑子里蹦出来的第一件事，虽然很烂，珍娜，

1089
00:47:00.920 --> 00:47:03.740
but I'm really bad at lying.
但我真的不擅长撒谎。

1090
00:47:03.960 --> 00:47:04.700
I'm really bad.
我真的很差劲。

1091
00:47:05.420 --> 00:47:07.040
And my dad was the same way.
我爸爸也一样。

1092
00:47:07.220 --> 00:47:09.080
Like, a police officer might pull him over for speeding,
比如，警察可能会因为超速拦下他，

1093
00:47:09.080 --> 00:47:10.780
and he'd be like, yep, I was.
他会说，是的，我超速了。

1094
00:47:10.780 --> 00:47:11.360
You're correct.
你说得对。

1095
00:47:11.540 --> 00:47:12.280
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1096
00:47:12.360 --> 00:47:12.540
Yeah.
明白。

1097
00:47:12.900 --> 00:47:15.280
One time I was working at 1-800 DentiSt.
有一次我在1-800 DentiSt工作，

1098
00:47:15.460 --> 00:47:17.820
You know, I was in my 20s, and I had this 6 a.m.
那时我20多岁，我有个早上6点的

1099
00:47:17.960 --> 00:47:18.280
shift,
班，

1100
00:47:18.720 --> 00:47:19.880
and I overslept.
结果我睡过头了。

1101
00:47:20.300 --> 00:47:23.560
And my manager called me, and he was so nice.
我的经理给我打电话，他态度特别好。

1102
00:47:24.020 --> 00:47:25.080
I answered the phone.
我接了电话。

1103
00:47:25.240 --> 00:47:25.780
Pretty groggy.
当时还迷迷糊糊的。

1104
00:47:25.900 --> 00:47:26.420
