我把这事告诉了室友，她们说，他明明给了你台阶下。

1117
00:47:53.860 --> 00:47:54.160
Twice.
给了两次。

1118
00:47:54.360 --> 00:47:54.980
I know.
我知道。

1119
00:47:55.240 --> 00:47:56.380
And I was like, no, no.
我说，不，不。

1120
00:47:57.960 --> 00:48:01.840
Well, I have a crazy story about pretending to be sick, and it involves Molly Shannon.
对了，我有个关于装病的疯狂故事，和莫莉·香农有关。

1121
00:48:02.100 --> 00:48:02.260
What?
什么？

1122
00:48:02.260 --> 00:48:05.400
Speaking of Molly Shannon, who's come up twice now on this podcaSt.
说到莫莉·香农，她在我们播客里已经出现两次了。

1123
00:48:05.420 --> 00:48:05.960
What happened?
发生了什么？

1124
00:48:06.400 --> 00:48:06.960
All right.
好吧。

1125
00:48:07.140 --> 00:48:11.840
So when I first came to L.A., I was working as a typist for the Television Critics Association.
我刚到洛杉矶时，在电视评论家协会做打字员。

1126
00:48:12.780 --> 00:48:16.840
All the stars of all of the new TV shows gather.
所有新剧的明星都会聚在那里。

1127
00:48:17.100 --> 00:48:18.720
We've gone to them for The Office.
我们拍《办公室》的时候也去过。

1128
00:48:18.720 --> 00:48:25.680
And you do a panel, and you talk to the Television Critics Association about your new show, about what you're doing.
你会参加一个小组讨论，向电视评论家协会介绍你的新剧，谈谈你在做什么。

1129
00:48:25.900 --> 00:48:26.120
Yeah.
是的。

1130
00:48:26.300 --> 00:48:33.500
