然后他们很快就离开了。

1630
01:06:42.330 --> 01:06:45.870
I have to shout out the cleaner who says, sorry, sorry.
我得特别提一下那个说“抱歉，抱歉”的清洁工。

1631
01:06:46.210 --> 01:06:47.410
He was played by
他是由

1632
01:06:47.410 --> 01:06:48.730
Boris Kiefsky.
鲍里斯·基夫斯基饰演的。

1633
01:06:48.970 --> 01:06:52.050
He is so, so, so, so good.
他演得太好、太好、太好、太好了。

1634
01:06:52.470 --> 01:06:56.790
Do you know how hard it is to like nail an acting moment?
你知道要精准演绎那种表演时刻有多难吗？

1635
01:06:56.790 --> 01:07:00.810
Like that, with that amount of just casual reality.
就像那样，带着那种随意的真实感。

1636
01:07:01.530 --> 01:07:02.990
I so believed him.
我完全相信他了。

1637
01:07:03.470 --> 01:07:05.150
I believed the whole world that
我完全相信那个随着音乐响起、他们走进来时

1638
01:07:05.150 --> 01:07:07.490
was happening with the music and them coming in.
所呈现出的整个世界。

1639
01:07:07.810 --> 01:07:09.010
He was so good.
他演得太棒了。

1640
01:07:09.250 --> 01:07:10.470
They all were so good.
他们所有人都演得太棒了。

1641
01:07:11.090 --> 01:07:11.530
Amazing.
太赞了。

1642
01:07:11.890 --> 01:07:12.570
I loved it.
我超喜欢。

1643
01:07:12.650 --> 01:07:15.810
I love the detail, too, that really shows you how long they've been at work.
我也很喜欢这个细节，它真实地展现了他们工作了多久。

1644
01:07:15.930 --> 01:07:16.110
Because
因为

1645
01:07:16.110 --> 01:07:20.590
you know if you've been at work when the cleaning crew arrives, you're like, oh, crap, I got to go.
你知道，如果你在清洁工到达时还在工作，你就会想，糟了，我得走了。

1646
01:07:20.590 --> 01:07:20.950
Yeah.
没错。

1647
01:07:21.770 --> 01:07:25.130
Randy said that the music they were playing was from the Universal Music Library,
兰迪说他们放的音乐来自环球音乐库，

1648
01:07:25.150 --> 01:07:26.350
and it didn't cost us anything.
而且没花我们一分钱。

1649
01:07:27.070 --> 01:07:29.490
Angela, now you have your very famous talking head.
安吉拉，现在轮到你那个非常有名的采访镜头了。

1650
01:07:29.730 --> 01:07:31.310
Yes, people quote this at me.
是的，人们经常拿这个来引用我。

1651
01:07:32.090 --> 01:07:36.410
Angela Martin says, yes, I'm anxious to get off work, but let me be
安吉拉·马丁说，没错，我急着下班，但让我把话说

1652
01:07:36.410 --> 01:07:36.730
clear.
清楚。

1653
01:07:37.210 --> 01:07:39.430
It's not to celebrate St. Patrick's Day.
我不是为了庆祝圣帕特里克节。

1654
01:07:39.570 --> 01:07:42.110
It's so I can protest St. Patrick's Day.
我是为了去抗议圣帕特里克节。

1655
01:07:42.110 --> 01:07:42.550
Hmm.
嗯。

1656
01:07:42.930 --> 01:07:44.130
How does one do that?
那要怎么做呢？

1657
01:07:44.910 --> 01:07:47.070
Well, this talking head was actually longer.
其实这段采访原本更长。

1658
01:07:47.270 --> 01:07:47.570
Oh.
噢。

1659
01:07:47.850 --> 01:07:48.710
And in the shooting
在拍摄

1660
01:07:48.710 --> 01:07:53.830
draft, she went on to say, a group of friends and I meet up with signs and travel from bar to bar.
草稿里，她接着说，我和一群朋友会拿着标语牌，一家酒吧一家酒吧地转。

1661
01:07:54.210 --> 01:07:55.990
I really look forward to it.
我真的很期待。

1662
01:07:56.530 --> 01:07:57.290
I love it.
我喜欢这样。

1663
01:07:57.490 --> 01:08:00.530
So there were a few candy bag alts for this talking head.
所以这段采访还有几个备选方案。

1664
01:08:00.650 --> 01:08:00.730
I'm
我

1665
01:08:00.730 --> 01:08:03.250
going to read you two of them, because you know, they were like a page and a half.
要读给你们听两个，因为你知道，它们大概有一页半长。

1666
01:08:04.370 --> 01:08:06.050
One is so odd.
其中一个太奇怪了。

1667
01:08:06.170 --> 01:08:06.270
It's
是

1668
01:08:06.270 --> 01:08:07.350
about the Steamtown Mall.
关于蒸汽镇购物中心的。

1669
01:08:07.490 --> 01:08:10.550
The other one I'm calling, is this a snarky writer moment?
另一个我称之为，这是编剧在耍贫嘴吗？

1670
01:08:10.930 --> 01:08:11.330
Oh,
噢，

1671
01:08:11.570 --> 01:08:12.490
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

1672
01:08:12.690 --> 01:08:14.970
Sometimes we would read things and we're like, hey.
有时候我们读到一些东西会觉得，嘿。

1673
01:08:16.250 --> 01:08:18.850
The first one, Angela Martin says,
第一个，安吉拉·马丁说，

1674
01:08:19.050 --> 01:08:21.950
I'm anxious to leave work to get to the Steamtown Mall.
我急着下班去蒸汽镇购物中心。

1675
01:08:22.230 --> 01:08:24.690
It's always empty on St. Patrick's Day,
圣帕特里克节那天那里总是空荡荡的，

1676
01:08:24.810 --> 01:08:26.930
